nt errors in the week''s main form; meaning sometimes unclear","onTarget":"The week''s main form used correctly at least once; errors do not block meaning","beyondTarget":"Main and light forms used accurately and flexibly; some longer, linked sentences"},{"key":"coherence","label":"Coherence","gettingThere":"Isolated sentences; few or no linking words","onTarget":"A clear order with basic linkers (then, so, because, since then, apart from that)","beyondTarget":"Ideas develop logically with varied linkers and clear signposting"}],"notes":["Not marked automatically: pronunciation and accent. The AI never treats an accent, or a word its speech recognition misheard, as a grammar or vocabulary error. Long pauses are not penalised; where a teacher reviews a recording, they may comment on fluency and pronunciation.","Confidence. If the AI''s bands are uncertain, or the transcript quality is poor, the recording is flagged for teacher review where a teacher is available, and the learner sees \"Feedback may be less accurate for this recording\"."],"learnerFeedback":["1. A band for each criterion.","2. One strength, quoting the learner''s own words.","3. One specific correction, prioritising the week''s main grammar point, with the corrected sentence.","4. A prompt to record again."],"recordings":"Four model answers, British English, natural pace (about 130-150 words a minute), with transcripts; 12 shadowing clips at normal and 0.8 speed with transcripts."},"placement":{"durationMinutes":35,"intro":"Placement takes about 35 minutes at sign-up and sends each learner to the foundation course, Stage 1 or Stage 2. The EF SET starting test is taken alongside it as the progress baseline, but placement makes the decision.","parts":[{"part":"Placement test","time":"15 min","what":"24 questions: 10 grammar, 6 vocabulary, 4 reading (one short text), 4 listening (two short clips)","markedBy":"App"},{"part":"Speaking sample","time":"3 min","what":"''Tell me about your job or studies, and what you''d like to be doing in two years'' time.'' 60 seconds, 30 seconds to plan.","markedBy":"AI, on the placement scale"},{"part":"Writing sample","time":"15 min","what":"''Write 80–100 words about a recent trip or event: what happened and what you enjoyed most.''","markedBy":"AI, on the placement scale"}],"questionBlueprint":[{"level":"A2","questions":6,"focus":"Past simple, comparatives, can / have to, everyday vocabulary"},{"level":"B1","questions":8,"focus":"Present perfect vs past simple, future forms, first conditional, modals, B1 vocabulary"},{"level":"B1+","questions":6,"focus":"Past perfect, passive, second conditional, relative clauses, collocations"},{"level":"B2","questions":4,"focus":"Reported speech, third conditional, modals of deduction, B2 vocabulary"}],"bands":[{"band":"A2","description":"''Getting there'' on most criteria: short, simple sentences; frequent errors that sometimes block meaning."},{"band":"B1","description":"''On target'' on most criteria: the task is done clearly; errors do not block meaning."},{"band":"B1+","description":"''Beyond target'' on most criteria: some range and longer, linked sentences."},{"band":"B2","description":"''Beyond target'' on all criteria: wide range, accurate complex sentences, well organised."}],"decisionRules":[{"outcome":"Foundation course","testScore":"0–11","samples":"Or both samples at A2, whatever the test score."},{"outcome":"Stage 1","testScore":"12–18","samples":"At least one sample at B1 or above."},{"outcome":"Stage 2","testScore":"19–24","samples":"Both samples at B1+ or above."}],"borderline":"If the score is within one point of a boundary, or the test and samples point to different results, place the learner in the lower option and tell them they can take a short move-up check after week 2. Where a teacher is involved, they review borderline cases first.","learnerChoice":"A learner placed in Stage 2 may choose to start at Stage 1. A learner placed in the foundation course is shown why, with links to suitable A2 material.","efSetCrossCheck":"If the EF SET result differs from the placement by a full CEFR level or more, the placement is flagged for review; it is not changed automatically."},"checkpoint1":{"intro":"A course checkpoint, not a CEFR placement or certification test. It assesses B1 grammar, a short spoken narrative and a 150-word piece, and is reported beside the learner''s EF SET starting test.","quiz":{"scoredItems":20,"reserveItems":4,"blueprint":"Four Main items and one Light item per week, written separately from the practice item bank so the checkpoint tests learning, not memory of practice items. Order: weeks 1–4, Main then Light. Exclude stretch tasks.","delivery":"Each item is auto-marked; the reason is shown only after the whole checkpoint is submitted. Short scenarios and answer keys allow valid variants; if two options are grammatical, ask which better expresses the stated meaning or accept both.","reporting":"Report results by skill and recommend a specific practice item."},"items":[{"id":"CP1-01","week":1,"target":"Main: finished time","prompt":"We ___ the Colosseum when we were in Rome in 2019.","options":["visited","have visited"],"key":"visited","reason":"''In 2019'' is a finished time."},{"id":"CP1-02","week":1,"target":"Main: past to now","prompt":"My brother ___ three different jobs since he left university.","options":["had","has had"],"key":"has had","reason":"''Since he left'' connects the past to now."},{"id":"CP1-03","week":1,"target":"Main: background","prompt":"The sun ___ (shine) when we left the hotel.","options":[],"key":"was shining","reason":"Background to the main event."},{"id":"CP1-04","week":1,"target":"Main: sequence","prompt":"When I opened the fridge, I realised someone ___ (eat) my cake.","options":[],"key":"had eaten","reason":"It happened before I opened the fridge."},{"id":"CP1-05","week":1,"target":"Light","prompt":"As a teenager, I ___ have very long hair.","options":["used to","would"],"key":"used to","reason":"''Have'' (possession) is a state, so would is not possible."},{"id":"CP1-06","week":2,"target":"Main: intention","prompt":"A: Any plans for the summer? B: I ___ visit my cousins in Ireland, but I haven''t booked anything yet.","options":["''m going to","''m visiting"],"key":"''m going to","reason":"An intention with nothing arranged yet."},{"id":"CP1-07","week":2,"target":"Main: arrangement","prompt":"We ___ (fly) to Lisbon on Friday. The tickets are in my bag.","options":[],"key":"''re flying (are flying)","reason":"A fixed arrangement."},{"id":"CP1-08","week":2,"target":"Main: time clause","prompt":"I''ll send you the photos when I ___ home.","options":["get","''ll get"],"key":"get","reason":"After ''when'', use the present simple for the future."},{"id":"CP1-09","week":2,"target":"Main: time clause","prompt":"As soon as the film ___ (finish), we''ll go for dinner.","options":[],"key":"finishes","reason":"After ''as soon as'', use the present simple for the future."},{"id":"CP1-10","week":2,"target":"Light","prompt":"If I ___ the lottery, I''d buy a house by the sea.","options":["won","win"],"key":"won","reason":"Second conditional: an imagined situation."},{"id":"CP1-11","week":3,"target":"Main: obligation","prompt":"In the UK, you ___ drive on the left.","options":["have to","don''t have to"],"key":"have to","reason":"It is a rule."},{"id":"CP1-12","week":3,"target":"Main: advice","prompt":"If you want to improve your English, you ___ read a little every day.","options":["should","mustn''t"],"key":"should","reason":"Advice."},{"id":"CP1-13","week":3,"target":"Main: ability","prompt":"My grandmother ___ (can / not / use) a smartphone, so we phone her.","options":[],"key":"can''t use (cannot use)","reason":"Ability, negative."},{"id":"CP1-14","week":3,"target":"Main: permission","prompt":"___ I leave my bag here while I go to the toilet?","options":["Can","Must"],"key":"Can (Could)","reason":"Asking for permission."},{"id":"CP1-15","week":3,"target":"Light","prompt":"Put the words in order: Where / you / do / work?","options":[],"key":"Where do you work?","reason":"Auxiliary before the subject."},{"id":"CP1-16","week":4,"target":"Main: present passive","prompt":"Cheese ___ (make) from milk.","options":[],"key":"is made","reason":"A general fact; the cheese is the focus."},{"id":"CP1-17","week":4,"target":"Main: present passive","prompt":"Most of the city''s buses ___ by electricity now.","options":["are powered","power"],"key":"are powered","reason":"Something powers the buses."},{"id":"CP1-18","week":4,"target":"Main: past passive","prompt":"The first email ___ (send) in 1971.","options":[],"key":"was sent","reason":"Past passive."},{"id":"CP1-19","week":4,"target":"Main: past passive","prompt":"Our flight ___ because of the snow.","options":["was cancelled","cancelled"],"key":"was cancelled","reason":"The airline cancelled it."},{"id":"CP1-20","week":4,"target":"Light","prompt":"This is the hotel ___ we stayed last summer.","options":["where","who"],"key":"where","reason":"''Where'' for a place followed by a full clause."}],"reserves":[{"id":"CP1-R1","week":1,"target":"reserve","prompt":"I ___ (not / see) her since the wedding.","options":[],"key":"haven''t seen (have not seen)","reason":"Up to now with since."},{"id":"CP1-R2","week":2,"target":"reserve","prompt":"Don''t worry, I ___ (call) you before I ___ (leave).","options":[],"key":"''ll call ... leave","reason":"Will for the promise; present simple after before."},{"id":"CP1-R3","week":3,"target":"reserve","prompt":"You ___ (not / have to) come to the party if you''re tired.","options":[],"key":"don''t have to","reason":"It isn''t necessary."},{"id":"CP1-R4","week":4,"target":"reserve","prompt":"The Alhambra ___ (visit) by millions of people every year.","options":[],"key":"is visited","reason":"Present passive with by."}],"reserveUse":"Reserves replace an item that pilot data shows is unclear, or form a retake for learners repeating the checkpoint.","writing":{"prompts":[{"label":"A. A change I got used to","text":"Describe how life was before a change, what happened, what was difficult, and how things are now."},{"label":"B. A note for a visitor","text":"A friend is visiting your town for a weekend. Recommend what to see: include a regular event or custom, one fact about a place''s past, a comparison, and one piece of advice."}],"conditions":[{"id":"length","setting":"Length","value":"150 words (130–170 accepted)"},{"id":"time","setting":"Time","value":"30 minutes, with a visible timer"},{"id":"where","setting":"Where","value":"In the app; pasting disabled; no phrase bank or model"},{"id":"attempts","setting":"Attempts","value":"One submission; no revise-and-retry"},{"id":"marking","setting":"Marking","value":"AI bands on the four writing criteria straight away; a teacher confirms where one is involved, and the teacher''s mark counts"}]},"result":{"intro":"Results are reported by part and by week, never as pass or fail. Learners continue to week 5 whatever their result; the checkpoint guides practice, it does not block progress.","thresholds":[{"part":"Quiz","onTarget":"14 of 20 or more (70%)"},{"part":"Speaking","onTarget":"''On target'' or better on at least three criteria, and task achievement not at ''Getting there''"},{"part":"Writing","onTarget":"''On target'' or better on at least three criteria, and task achievement not at ''Getting there''"}],"practiceLinks":"Each part below target links to the matching practice: weak quiz items to that week''s extra items and grammar clinic, speaking to the week''s shadowing and conversation, writing to a revise-and-retry task on the same prompt."},"calibration":["A second teacher checks every checkpoint item for a single correct answer and accepted variants.","Check the existing 24 placement questions against the blueprint (6 A2, 8 B1, 6 B1+, 4 B2) and replace those that do not fit.","Mark 10–20 sample texts and recordings by hand and compare with the AI''s bands; adjust prompts until they agree on at least 8 in 10.","After 30 placed learners, compare placement with EF SET results and adjust the cut scores (11/12 and 18/19).","Review any checkpoint item that more than 90% or fewer than 30% of pilot learners answer correctly.","Confirm the checkpoint thresholds (70% quiz, three of four criteria) against teacher judgement of pilot learners."],"speaking":{"status":"pilot draft — pending second-teacher review","intro":"After week 4, learners record one short spoken narrative under checkpoint conditions, marked with the same four descriptors.","prompt":"Talk about a time when you had to adapt to something new: a job, a place, a course or a routine. What was it like before, what happened, and how are things now? If you like, say what you would tell someone in the same situation.","conditions":[{"setting":"Planning","value":"1 minute; notes allowed, no phrase bank or model"},{"setting":"Length","value":"60-90 seconds"},{"setting":"Attempts","value":"One recording; no retry (practice tasks allow retries, checkpoints do not)"},{"setting":"Marking","value":"AI bands on the four criteria straight away; a teacher confirms where one is involved, and the teacher''s mark counts"},{"setting":"On target","value":"\"On target\" or better on at least three of the four criteria, with no criterion at \"Getting there\" for task achievement"},{"setting":"Language it draws on","value":"Weeks 1-4: narrative tenses, present perfect, used to / would, modals for advice; featured vocabulary from any of the four weeks"}],"transferNote":"The prompt is new, so it tests transfer rather than memory of a practised answer."}},"status":"pilot draft — pending second-teacher review","sources":["Writing descriptors, placement and checkpoint 1 (21 Nov 2026)","Fluency Studio: Weeks 1–4 Speaking Content (21 Nov 2026)"]}'::jsonb->'checkpoint1')
